    "Property, plant and equipment is initially recognised at cost, including directly attributable expenditure and qualifying restoration obligations. The applicable cost or revaluation model is identified by class. Depreciable amounts are allocated over useful lives, with significant components depreciated separately. Useful lives, residual values and methods are reviewed at least at each financial year end. Disposals and impairment are accounted for under IAS 16 and IAS 36.",
    "An item of property, plant and equipment is derecognised on disposal or when no future economic benefits are expected. The gain or loss equals net disposal proceeds, if any, less the carrying amount and is recognised in profit or loss.",
    "Property, plant and equipment is initially recognised at cost, including directly attributable expenditure and qualifying restoration obligations. The applicable cost or revaluation model is identified by class. Depreciable amounts are allocated over useful lives, with significant components depreciated separately. Useful lives, residual values and methods are reviewed at least at each financial year end. Disposals and impairment are accounted for under IAS 16 and IAS 36."
